    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nMini.starter\n\n### Description\n\nI'd like to report an issue with Mini.starter. When I attempt to open bash/zsh/sh formatted files directly using the `nvim .example` command, I encounter an error. The error message initially prompts me to \"Press enter or type a command to continue.\" \r\n\r\nAfter pressing enter, I receive the following error: `(mini.starter) 'buf_id' in 'refresh()' is not a valid Starter buffer identifier.`\r\n\r\nPlease note that I observed a similar issue mentioned in #230, but the steps to reproduce it differ.\r\n\r\n\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.9.2\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. create any hidden file without file ext like **(.zshrc / .bzshrc / .examplerc)**\r\n2. copy this line to the file: `#!/bin/zsh` to tell it its sh format and write then close nvim.\r\n3. run this command in terminal to open the file `nvim .examplerc`\r\n4. the issue would appear\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n_No response_\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nA notification is sent by mini.starter saying \"buf_id in refresh() is not an identifier of valid Starter buffer\". This does not occur with the any other file or if you open the file `.zshrc` after opening neovim.",
